  "_comment": "Blue-chip watchlist universe, expanded in stages from the original v1 20-ticker seed. Tickers use Yahoo Finance symbol convention (.ST Nordic Sweden, .CO Copenhagen, .HE Helsinki, .OL Oslo, .SW SIX Swiss, .DE Xetra Germany, .L London, .PA Paris, .AS Amsterdam, .MI Milan, .MC Madrid, no suffix for US-listed). Regions: nordic = full OMXS30 (Sweden) + Indutrade; us = Dow 30 + mega-caps + a curated quality/healthcare/financial-infrastructure set; germany = top 20 DAX by market cap; uk = top ~20 FTSE 100 by market cap (AstraZeneca tracked once, via its Stockholm listing, not duplicated here); nordic_ex_sweden = Denmark/Finland/Norway large caps; switzerland = SIX blue chips (ABB deliberately excluded -- already tracked via its Stockholm listing ABB.ST); europe = France/Netherlands/Italy/Spain large caps (Vivendi deliberately excluded post-2024 breakup -- structure and coverage too unsettled); japan = the 3 Japanese names with clean, liquid US-listed tickers (Hitachi/Keyence deliberately excluded -- no good US ticker, would need native Tokyo .T symbols not yet used anywhere in this project); emerging_markets = liquid US-listed EM large caps (Tencent/TCEHY deliberately excluded -- OTC ADR, thinner data than an exchange listing). Nothing in the ingestion or scoring code is hardcoded to this list -- edit freely. region is used only for reporting/filtering, not scoring. Constituent lists and exchange suffixes are hand-researched/hand-mapped -- spot-check before relying on any single ticker, especially the newer non-Nordic/non-US/non-UK/non-German additions, which are less battle-tested than the original core.",
